WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

2
00:02:00.413 --> 00:02:03.291
You did this!

3
00:02:03.374 --> 00:02:06.377
- We have to leave.
- Take him!

4
00:02:09.339 --> 00:02:10.965
Where is his wife?

5
00:02:11.716 --> 00:02:12.759
Where's Sansa?

6
00:02:12.842 --> 00:02:17.305
Find her. Bar the gates of the city.
Seize every ship in the harbour.

7
00:02:18.806 --> 00:02:20.600
- Where is she?
- No one leaves the capital!

8
00:02:51.464 --> 00:02:52.882
Get in.

9
00:02:52.924 --> 00:02:54.444
- Where are we going?
- Somewhere safe.

10
00:03:40.805 --> 00:03:42.640
Up you go. my lady.

11
00:03:45.518 --> 00:03:46.978
You'll be fine.

12
00:03:47.061 --> 00:03:49.313
You're stronger than you know.

13
00:04:07.790 --> 00:04:09.542
- Lord Baelish?
- Petyr.

14
00:04:10.293 --> 00:04:11.669
Are you hurt. my lady?

15
00:04:12.295 --> 00:04:13.671
Good.

16
00:04:14.130 --> 00:04:16.507
I'm sure you've had quite a fright.
Rest easy.

17
00:04:16.549 --> 00:04:18.269
- The worst is past.
- Lord Baelish.

18
00:04:18.426 --> 00:04:21.012
- I promised I'd get her to you safely.
- Softly. my friend.

19
00:04:21.721 --> 00:04:23.931
Voices carry over water.

20
00:04:24.015 --> 00:04:26.768
I should get back before
someone thinks to look for me.

21
00:04:26.851 --> 00:04:29.020
First you'll want your pay.

22
00:04:29.061 --> 00:04:32.190
- Ten thousand. was it?
- Ten thousand.

23
00:04:37.487 --> 00:04:38.696
Wait!

24
00:04:41.032 --> 00:04:42.742
Shh.

25
00:04:42.825 --> 00:04:44.869
You don't want the Queen to hear. do you?

26
00:04:44.952 --> 00:04:47.914
A thousand gold cloaks
are searching for you.

27
00:04:47.997 --> 00:04:50.041
And if they found you.

28
00:04:50.082 --> 00:04:53.211
how do you think they would punish
the girl who murdered the King?

29
00:04:53.252 --> 00:04:55.171
I didn't murder anyone.

30
00:04:55.213 --> 00:04:57.882
I know. But you must admit.
it looks suspicious.

31
00:04:57.924 --> 00:04:59.926
The King who executed your father.

32
00:05:00.009 --> 00:05:02.220
who tormented you for years.

33
00:05:02.261 --> 00:05:04.764
and you fled the scene of his murder.

34
00:05:05.640 --> 00:05:07.099
Why did you kill him?

35
00:05:07.558 --> 00:05:09.852
Because he was a drunk and a fool.

36
00:05:09.894 --> 00:05:12.730
and I don't trust drunk fools.

37
00:05:13.731 --> 00:05:15.024
He saved me.

38
00:05:15.066 --> 00:05:19.153
Saved you? My lady. he followed my orders.
Every one of them.

39
00:05:19.654 --> 00:05:22.532
And he did it all for gold.

40
00:05:22.615 --> 00:05:25.076
Money buys a man's silence for a time.

41
00:05:25.409 --> 00:05:28.621
A bolt in the heart buys it forever.

42
00:05:31.082 --> 00:05:33.751
He was helping me because I saved his life.

43
00:05:33.793 --> 00:05:37.713
Yes. and he gave you a priceless necklace

44
00:05:38.130 --> 00:05:40.925
that once belonged to his grandmother.

45
00:05:41.175 --> 00:05:43.803
The last legacy of House Hollard.

46
00:05:52.520 --> 00:05:54.605
I had it made a few weeks ago.

47
00:05:56.148 --> 00:05:59.068
What did I once tell you about the capital?

48
00:05:59.819 --> 00:06:01.737
"We're all liars here."

49
00:06:03.614 --> 00:06:05.491
Come. my lady.

50
00:06:05.575 --> 00:06:07.785
I know you've had a difficult day.

51
00:06:08.536 --> 00:06:10.580
But you're safe now.

52
00:06:10.621 --> 00:06:12.707
I promise you that.

53
00:06:12.790 --> 00:06:15.543
You're safe with me.

54
00:06:15.626 --> 00:06:18.087
sailing home.

55
00:06:23.718 --> 00:06:25.928
So am I the queen?

56
00:06:26.220 --> 00:06:27.972
More than you were with Renly.

57
00:06:28.055 --> 00:06:29.307
Less than you would have been

58
00:06:29.390 --> 00:06:33.978
if Joffrey had done you the courtesy
of consummating the marriage before dying.

59
00:06:34.478 --> 00:06:38.941
This would not be
an opportune moment to press the issue.

60
00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:42.820
Clawing at his own throat.
looking to his mother to make it stop...

61
00:06:42.862 --> 00:06:43.905
It was horrible.

62
00:06:43.988 --> 00:06:46.324
The world is overflowing
with horrible things.

63
00:06:46.407 --> 00:06:48.247
But they're all a tray
of cakes next to death.

64
00:06:50.328 --> 00:06:53.414
They brought me your grandfather's body
when he died.

65
00:06:53.497 --> 00:06:55.207
Made me look at it.

66
00:06:55.333 --> 00:06:56.792
What was it like?

67
00:06:56.834 --> 00:06:59.962
They took me to the Great Hall.
There he was.

68
00:07:00.713 --> 00:07:04.675
The man I'd married
and suffered to father my children.

69
00:07:05.301 --> 00:07:10.890
A great doughy lump I'd sat next to
at endless dinners and tedious gatherings.

70
00:07:11.390 --> 00:07:12.516
There he was.

71
00:07:14.268 --> 00:07:16.020
lying on a table.

72
00:07:19.857 --> 00:07:22.151
One of my husbands
preferred the company of men

73
00:07:22.193 --> 00:07:24.111
and was stabbed through the heart.

74
00:07:24.195 --> 00:07:26.364
Another was happiest torturing animals

75
00:07:26.447 --> 00:07:28.783
and was poisoned at our wedding feast.

76
00:07:28.908 --> 00:07:30.576
- I must be cursed.
- Nonsense.

77
00:07:30.785 --> 00:07:33.496
Your circumstances have improved markedly.

78
00:07:35.498 --> 00:07:38.250
You may not have enjoyed watching him die.

79
00:07:38.334 --> 00:07:40.187
but you enjoyed it more
than you would have enjoyed

80
00:07:40.211 --> 00:07:42.171
being married to him.
I can promise you that.

81
00:07:42.296 --> 00:07:44.298
But I would have been the queen.

82
00:07:44.382 --> 00:07:46.384
Our alliance with the Lannisters

83
00:07:46.467 --> 00:07:49.929
remains every bit as necessary to them
as it is unpleasant for us.

84
00:07:51.722 --> 00:07:54.308
You did wonderful work on Joffrey.

85
00:07:54.684 --> 00:07:56.727
The next one should be easier.

86
00:08:07.363 --> 00:08:08.906
Your brother is dead.

87
00:08:10.825 --> 00:08:12.994
Do you know what that means?

88
00:08:16.080 --> 00:08:18.416
I'm not trying to trick you.

89
00:08:20.501 --> 00:08:22.294
It means I'll become king.

90
00:08:22.378 --> 00:08:25.589
Yes. you will become king.

91
00:08:25.631 --> 00:08:27.842
What kind of king do you think you'll be?

92
00:08:29.301 --> 00:08:31.345
- A good king?
- Mmm.

93
00:08:31.554 --> 00:08:33.472
I think so as well.

94
00:08:34.890 --> 00:08:37.685
You've got the right temperament for it.

95
00:08:38.686 --> 00:08:41.147
But what makes a good king? Hmm?

96
00:08:41.981 --> 00:08:45.026
What is a good king's
single most important quality?

97
00:08:45.109 --> 00:08:47.069
This is hardly the place or the time.

98
00:08:48.112 --> 00:08:50.114
- Holiness?
- Hmm.

99
00:08:52.450 --> 00:08:54.660
Baelor the Blessed was holy.

100
00:08:55.077 --> 00:08:56.871
And pious.

101
00:08:56.954 --> 00:08:58.622
He built this Sept.

102
00:08:59.665 --> 00:09:02.793
He also named a 6-year-old boy High Septon

103
00:09:02.835 --> 00:09:05.963
because he thought
the boy could work miracles.

104
00:09:07.465 --> 00:09:10.134
He ended up
fasting himself into an early grave

105
00:09:10.217 --> 00:09:14.472
because food was of this world
and this world was sinful.

106
00:09:14.555 --> 00:09:15.598
Hmm.

107
00:09:17.349 --> 00:09:19.268
- Justice.
- Mmm.

108
00:09:20.394 --> 00:09:22.480
A good king must be just.

109
00:09:23.689 --> 00:09:26.484
Orys I was just.

110
00:09:26.567 --> 00:09:29.028
Everyone applauded his reforms.

111
00:09:29.111 --> 00:09:31.155
nobles and commoners alike.

112
00:09:31.197 --> 00:09:33.365
But he wasn't just for long.

113
00:09:34.116 --> 00:09:37.661
He was murdered in his sleep
after less than a year by his own brother.

114
00:09:38.996 --> 00:09:40.873
Was that truly just of him?

115
00:09:40.956 --> 00:09:45.461
To abandon his subjects to an evil that
he was too gullible to recognise?

116
00:09:45.669 --> 00:09:47.797
- No.
- No.

117
00:09:50.216 --> 00:09:53.010
- What about strength?
- Yes.

118
00:09:53.052 --> 00:09:55.304
Strength.

119
00:09:55.346 --> 00:09:58.182
King Robert was strong.

120
00:09:58.224 --> 00:10:00.309
He won the rebellion

121
00:10:00.351 --> 00:10:03.145
and crushed the Targaryen dynasty.

122
00:10:04.105 --> 00:10:08.609
And he attended three Small Council
meetings in 17 years.

123
00:10:08.776 --> 00:10:12.988
He spent his time whoring and hunting
and drinking

124
00:10:13.072 --> 00:10:15.366
until the last two killed him.

125
00:10:16.784 --> 00:10:20.037
So. we have a man
who starves himself to death.

126
00:10:20.454 --> 00:10:23.624
a man who lets his own brother murder him.

127
00:10:23.707 --> 00:10:27.169
and a man who thinks that winning and ruling
are the same thing.

128
00:10:30.005 --> 00:10:32.133
What do they all lack?

129
00:10:36.887 --> 00:10:38.514
- Wisdom.
- Yes!

130
00:10:38.764 --> 00:10:41.267
- Wisdom is what makes a good king.
- Yes.

131
00:10:42.685 --> 00:10:45.229
But what is wisdom? Hmm?

132
00:10:47.523 --> 00:10:51.777
A house with great wealth and fertile lands
asks you for your protection

133
00:10:51.861 --> 00:10:57.158
against another house with a strong navy
that could one day oppose you.

134
00:10:57.950 --> 00:11:00.661
How do you know
which choice is wise and which isn't?

135
00:11:01.203 --> 00:11:04.623
You've any experience
of treasuries and granaries

136
00:11:04.707 --> 00:11:07.418
or shipyards and soldiers?

137
00:11:07.459 --> 00:11:09.879
- No.
- Of course not.

138
00:11:10.254 --> 00:11:13.299
A wise king knows what he knows
and what he doesn't.

139
00:11:14.091 --> 00:11:15.134
You're young.

140
00:11:15.885 --> 00:11:21.891
A wise young king listens to his counsellors
and heeds their advice until he comes of age.

141
00:11:22.266 --> 00:11:24.185
And the wisest kings

142
00:11:24.268 --> 00:11:27.313
continue to listen to them long afterwards.

143
00:11:29.231 --> 00:11:30.774
Your brother was not a wise king.

144
00:11:31.275 --> 00:11:33.319
Your brother was not a good king.

145
00:11:33.402 --> 00:11:35.446
If he had been.

146
00:11:35.529 --> 00:11:38.115
perhaps he'd still be alive.

147
00:11:38.199 --> 00:11:41.160
Now. as the king. you will have to marry.

148
00:11:42.119 --> 00:11:43.662
Do you understand why?

149
00:11:43.746 --> 00:11:45.289
A king needs a queen.

150
00:11:45.372 --> 00:11:47.208
Yes. but why?

151
00:11:48.209 --> 00:11:50.961
To further the family line.

152
00:11:51.170 --> 00:11:53.214
- Do you know how that happens?
- Yes.

153
00:11:54.215 --> 00:11:57.968
But has anyone
explained the details to you?

154
00:11:58.052 --> 00:11:59.637
I don't think so.

155
00:11:59.678 --> 00:12:02.431
It's all relatively straightforward.

156
00:12:03.015 --> 00:12:05.643
- How are you?
- I'm all right.

157
00:12:05.726 --> 00:12:07.519
You are. You will be.

158
00:12:07.811 --> 00:12:09.605
I'll see to that.

159
00:12:15.027 --> 00:12:17.112
Please give the Queen
a moment alone with her son.

160
00:12:17.196 --> 00:12:19.531
- Yes. my lord.
- All of you.

161
00:12:48.394 --> 00:12:50.521
It was Tyrion.

162
00:12:52.231 --> 00:12:53.649
He killed him.

163
00:12:55.526 --> 00:12:57.653
He told me he would.

164
00:12:59.029 --> 00:13:03.200
"A day will come when you
think you are safe and happy.

165
00:13:03.242 --> 00:13:06.787
"and your joy will turn to ashes
in your mouth."

166
00:13:09.290 --> 00:13:11.583
That's what he said to me.

167
00:13:14.920 --> 00:13:16.588
You saw it.

168
00:13:17.923 --> 00:13:21.093
- You saw Joff point at him just before he...
- I don't know what I saw.

169
00:13:24.722 --> 00:13:27.057
Avenge him.

170
00:13:27.641 --> 00:13:30.060
Avenge our son.

171
00:13:31.645 --> 00:13:32.646
Kill Tyrion.

172
00:13:35.858 --> 00:13:37.568
Tyrion's my brother.

173
00:13:37.651 --> 00:13:39.236
Our brother.

174
00:13:39.737 --> 00:13:42.048
There'll be a trial.
We'll get to the truth of what happened.

175
00:13:42.072 --> 00:13:44.575
I don't want a trial.

176
00:13:44.616 --> 00:13:47.911
He'll squirm his way to freedom
given the chance.

177
00:13:48.078 --> 00:13:49.621
I want him dead.

178
00:13:52.833 --> 00:13:56.420
Please. Jaime. You have to.

179
00:13:58.630 --> 00:14:01.008
He was our son.

180
00:14:01.091 --> 00:14:03.093
Our baby boy.

181
00:14:42.800 --> 00:14:45.302
You're a hateful woman.

182
00:14:45.344 --> 00:14:47.679
Why have the gods made me
love a hateful woman?

183
00:14:55.979 --> 00:14:57.231
Jaime. not here. please.

184
00:14:58.357 --> 00:14:59.858
Please.

185
00:15:00.609 --> 00:15:01.819
Stop it.

186
00:15:01.860 --> 00:15:03.946
- Stop it.
- No.

187
00:15:05.114 --> 00:15:07.449
Stop it.

188
00:15:11.829 --> 00:15:12.996
Stop.

189
00:15:21.255 --> 00:15:23.465
Stop. It's not right.

190
00:15:24.842 --> 00:15:27.177
It's not right.

191
00:15:27.219 --> 00:15:29.221
I don't care.

192
00:15:29.304 --> 00:15:30.722
- Don't.
- I don't care.

193
00:15:31.140 --> 00:15:33.016
- Jaime. don't.
- I don't care.

194
00:15:35.853 --> 00:15:37.729
Gonna rain soon.

195
00:15:40.357 --> 00:15:42.025
Where are we?

196
00:15:44.695 --> 00:15:47.156
Near Fairmarket. I think.

197
00:15:47.656 --> 00:15:48.699
You think?

198
00:15:48.740 --> 00:15:50.200
You don't have a map?

199
00:15:50.284 --> 00:15:53.370
- No.
- Maybe we should get one.

200
00:15:53.412 --> 00:15:56.540
Just point out the next map shop
you see. and I'll buy you one.

201
00:15:56.582 --> 00:15:59.626
- How far is it to the Eyrie?
- Far.

202
00:15:59.710 --> 00:16:01.312
And you're sure we're going the right way?

203
00:16:01.336 --> 00:16:04.882
Believe me. girl.
I want you there as soon as I can.

204
00:16:04.923 --> 00:16:07.384
Get my gold. be on my way.

205
00:16:07.426 --> 00:16:10.137
- Where?
- Why do you care?

206
00:16:16.810 --> 00:16:20.022
Might book passage across the Narrow Sea.

207
00:16:20.063 --> 00:16:21.899
Fight as a sellsword.

208
00:16:22.357 --> 00:16:24.693
Second Sons. could be.

209
00:16:24.735 --> 00:16:26.862
Seems like a good fit for me.

210
00:16:26.904 --> 00:16:28.447
I'd like to see Braavos one day.

211
00:16:28.530 --> 00:16:29.740
Why Braavos?

212
00:16:31.492 --> 00:16:32.576
I have friends there.

213
00:16:33.035 --> 00:16:34.703
I doubt it.

214
00:16:34.912 --> 00:16:36.330
Seven blessings to you.

215
00:16:39.583 --> 00:16:42.836
- What do you want?
- This is my land.

216
00:16:42.920 --> 00:16:44.963
If I'm standing on it. it's my land.

217
00:16:45.047 --> 00:16:48.217
We were just watering the horses.
We'll be on our way.

218
00:16:52.763 --> 00:16:54.264
Forgive my father.

219
00:16:54.306 --> 00:16:56.725
He was wounded fighting in the war.

220
00:16:56.767 --> 00:16:59.811
Our cottage burned down while he was gone.
and my mother with it.

221
00:17:03.774 --> 00:17:05.192
He's never been the same.

222
00:17:10.781 --> 00:17:11.949
Which house did he fight for?

223
00:17:17.788 --> 00:17:19.289
The Tullys of Riverrun.

224
00:17:23.752 --> 00:17:25.128
There's a storm coming.

225
00:17:25.212 --> 00:17:26.672
You'll be wanting a roof tonight.

226
00:17:27.089 --> 00:17:28.924
There's fresh hay in the barn.

227
00:17:28.966 --> 00:17:31.843
And Sally here makes rabbit stew
just like her mom used to do.

228
00:17:34.596 --> 00:17:38.684
We don't have much. but any man that
bled for House Tully is welcome to it.

229
00:17:43.855 --> 00:17:48.318
We ask the Father to judge us
with mercy. accepting our human frailty.

230
00:17:48.569 --> 00:17:50.487
We ask the Mother to bless our crops.

231
00:17:50.529 --> 00:17:53.574
so we may feed ourselves
and all who come to our door.

232
00:17:53.657 --> 00:17:57.828
We ask the Warrior to give us courage
in these days of strife and turmoil.

233
00:17:57.911 --> 00:18:00.205
We ask the Maiden to protect Sally's virtue

234
00:18:00.289 --> 00:18:01.975
and keep her from the clutches of depravity.

235
00:18:01.999 --> 00:18:03.750
You going to do all seven of the fuckers?

236
00:18:04.126 --> 00:18:05.168
Father!

237
00:18:09.673 --> 00:18:12.676
We ask the Smith to strengthen our hands
and our backs.

238
00:18:12.759 --> 00:18:14.928
so we may finish the work required of us.

239
00:18:15.053 --> 00:18:19.016
We ask the Crone to guide us on our journey
from darkness to darkness.

240
00:18:19.099 --> 00:18:23.645
And we ask the Stranger not to kill us
in our beds tonight for no damn reason at all.

241
00:18:29.359 --> 00:18:30.694
I'm so sorry.

242
00:18:50.714 --> 00:18:51.715
Really good.

243
00:18:52.466 --> 00:18:53.651
Did you fight at the Twins?

244
00:18:53.675 --> 00:18:57.262
Call that a fight?
Slaughtering livestock more like.

245
00:18:57.346 --> 00:19:00.098
The Red Wedding. they're calling it.

246
00:19:00.182 --> 00:19:02.267
Walder Frey committed sacrilege that day.

247
00:19:02.392 --> 00:19:05.729
He shared bread and salt with the Starks.
He offered them guest right.

248
00:19:05.812 --> 00:19:07.814
Guest right don't mean much any more.

249
00:19:07.898 --> 00:19:10.150
It means something to me.

250
00:19:11.276 --> 00:19:13.236
The gods will have their vengeance.

251
00:19:13.737 --> 00:19:15.737
Frey will burn in the seventh hell
for what he did.

252
00:19:17.074 --> 00:19:19.868
Things were different
when Hoster Tully ruled the Riverlands.

253
00:19:19.910 --> 00:19:23.205
We had good years and bad years.
same as anyone. but we were safe.

254
00:19:23.538 --> 00:19:25.457
Now with the Freys.

255
00:19:25.540 --> 00:19:29.336
raiders come plundering.
steal our food. steal our silver.

256
00:19:29.419 --> 00:19:31.546
I was gonna send Sally north
to stay with my brother.

257
00:19:31.588 --> 00:19:34.591
but the North's no better.
The whole country's gone sour.

258
00:19:35.258 --> 00:19:36.426
You got any ale?

259
00:19:38.011 --> 00:19:39.471
Afraid not.

260
00:19:43.058 --> 00:19:45.102
How can a man not keep ale in his home?

261
00:19:47.437 --> 00:19:50.190
You look like
you could really swing that sword.

262
00:19:50.273 --> 00:19:52.442
A real warrior with proper training.

263
00:19:53.944 --> 00:19:56.655
Those raiders wouldn't
stand a chance against you.

264
00:19:57.280 --> 00:19:59.280
How would it be
if you stayed on till the new moon?

265
00:19:59.658 --> 00:20:02.119
I could use a man to help
with the farm work.

266
00:20:02.202 --> 00:20:04.538
Sally does what she can.

267
00:20:04.621 --> 00:20:06.206
but she can't lift a bale of hay.

268
00:20:06.832 --> 00:20:09.000
And if any thieves came
looking for easy pickings.

269
00:20:09.084 --> 00:20:11.837
one look at you.
I bet they'd run the other way.

270
00:20:13.797 --> 00:20:15.132
Meaning no offence.

271
00:20:22.097 --> 00:20:23.432
What'll you pay?

272
00:20:24.141 --> 00:20:26.518
I don't have much.

273
00:20:26.601 --> 00:20:28.937
But I have hidden a bit of silver
from the bandits.

274
00:20:31.648 --> 00:20:32.816
Fair wages for fair work?

275
00:20:39.865 --> 00:20:41.533
Fair wages for fair work.

276
00:21:01.470 --> 00:21:02.804
Ahhh!

277
00:21:14.191 --> 00:21:16.693
- What did you do?
- Get your horse saddled.

278
00:21:16.777 --> 00:21:19.696
- You told me you weren't a thief.
- I wasn't.

279
00:21:19.780 --> 00:21:22.365
He took us in. He fed us and you...

280
00:21:22.407 --> 00:21:25.869
Aye. he took us in. He's a good man.
and his daughter makes a nice stew.

281
00:21:25.952 --> 00:21:27.871
And they'll both be dead come winter.

282
00:21:27.913 --> 00:21:30.207
- You don't know that.
- I do.

283
00:21:30.290 --> 00:21:33.502
He's weak. He can't protect himself.

284
00:21:33.543 --> 00:21:35.837
They'll both be dead come winter.

285
00:21:35.879 --> 00:21:37.422
Dead men don't need silver.

286
00:21:38.006 --> 00:21:41.968
You're the worst shit in the Seven Kingdoms.

287
00:21:42.761 --> 00:21:44.971
There's plenty worse than me.

288
00:21:45.055 --> 00:21:47.724
I just understand the way things are.

289
00:21:47.808 --> 00:21:50.602
How many Starks they got to behead
before you figure it out?

290
00:21:55.065 --> 00:21:58.109
Raper.

291
00:21:58.193 --> 00:21:59.694
Horse thief.

292
00:21:59.736 --> 00:22:01.363
Ninth-born son.

293
00:22:02.239 --> 00:22:04.825
Raper. Thief.

294
00:22:04.908 --> 00:22:06.910
Thief and raper.

295
00:22:06.993 --> 00:22:09.454
There he is. Sam the Slayer.

296
00:22:09.538 --> 00:22:11.873
Going to visit your wildling whore?

297
00:22:11.915 --> 00:22:13.625
- She's not a whore.
- No?

298
00:22:13.708 --> 00:22:16.086
Maybe I'll give her a copper tonight
and find out.

299
00:22:21.591 --> 00:22:23.635
They all think I'm lying.

300
00:22:23.718 --> 00:22:25.595
About what?

301
00:22:25.679 --> 00:22:27.681
Killing the White Walker.

302
00:22:27.764 --> 00:22:29.307
You're not lying.

303
00:22:30.183 --> 00:22:32.060
I'll never forget the way it screamed.

304
00:22:34.312 --> 00:22:36.147
But you're the only one that saw it.

305
00:22:36.231 --> 00:22:37.858
And they all think you're just a...

306
00:22:37.941 --> 00:22:39.109
A what?

307
00:22:39.150 --> 00:22:42.112
A wildling.

308
00:22:43.446 --> 00:22:45.282
My father hated that word.

309
00:22:45.866 --> 00:22:49.953
- It's not a very nice word.
- I don't know.

310
00:22:50.954 --> 00:22:54.249
It makes me sound a bit dangerous.
doesn't it?

311
00:23:06.469 --> 00:23:09.890
So. are you all right?

312
00:23:09.973 --> 00:23:12.350
No one bothering you?

313
00:23:12.434 --> 00:23:14.227
I get a lot of looks.

314
00:23:14.311 --> 00:23:16.229
I hear them making their jokes.

315
00:23:16.313 --> 00:23:19.149
But no one's touched me.
if that's what you mean.

316
00:23:20.358 --> 00:23:22.319
I worry about it sometimes.

317
00:23:22.986 --> 00:23:24.779
All the time.

318
00:23:25.322 --> 00:23:27.657
Why do you worry about it?

319
00:23:27.699 --> 00:23:30.994
One hundred men. one woman.

320
00:23:31.077 --> 00:23:33.538
They've got other things to think about.

321
00:23:33.622 --> 00:23:35.665
That's the only thing they think about.

322
00:23:35.707 --> 00:23:38.919
- You're being silly.
- I'm not being silly.

323
00:23:39.002 --> 00:23:42.839
There's 100 men lying awake at night.
picturing you.

324
00:23:44.174 --> 00:23:46.092
What about you?

325
00:23:48.178 --> 00:23:49.554
What about me?

326
00:23:52.849 --> 00:23:54.184
Gilly?

327
00:23:59.689 --> 00:24:01.524
I worry about you.

328
00:24:06.529 --> 00:24:08.031
Thank you.

329
00:24:08.573 --> 00:24:09.616
For what?

330
00:24:09.699 --> 00:24:11.826
For worrying about me.

331
00:24:15.830 --> 00:24:18.917
I don't know if you're safe here.

332
00:24:19.918 --> 00:24:21.211
They're my brothers.

333
00:24:21.294 --> 00:24:23.630
but some of them were thieves
before they came here.

334
00:24:23.713 --> 00:24:25.882
Some of them were rapers.

335
00:24:25.924 --> 00:24:28.051
You saw what they did at your father's keep.

336
00:24:29.302 --> 00:24:30.887
So what are you saying?

337
00:24:34.224 --> 00:24:38.895
Maybe you'd be safer in Mole's Town.

338
00:24:43.608 --> 00:24:45.819
Are you bored of me?

339
00:24:46.736 --> 00:24:47.779
Bored of you?

340
00:24:48.863 --> 00:24:50.156
I...

341
00:24:54.577 --> 00:24:56.371
I want to protect you.

342
00:25:03.086 --> 00:25:05.005
I'll get these to Hobb.

343
00:25:05.088 --> 00:25:07.257
Keep an eye on little Sam.

344
00:25:37.162 --> 00:25:38.830
Your Grace.

345
00:25:39.289 --> 00:25:42.292
You're a literary man now.
What do you make of that?

346
00:25:52.469 --> 00:25:56.097
- Joffrey?
- "The usurper. Joffrey Baratheon."

347
00:25:56.347 --> 00:25:59.184
I said those words
when I tossed a leech into the fire.

348
00:25:59.350 --> 00:26:01.978
filled with bastard blood.

349
00:26:02.145 --> 00:26:03.813
A bastard you set free.

350
00:26:04.564 --> 00:26:07.025
I am now faced with a great opportunity.

351
00:26:07.108 --> 00:26:08.985
and I am powerless to take advantage of it.

352
00:26:09.027 --> 00:26:10.212
I will find you an army. Your Grace.

353
00:26:10.236 --> 00:26:12.876
- I've been working day and night...
- What progress have you made?

354
00:26:13.364 --> 00:26:16.159
- I've rallied House Peasebury to your cause.
- House Peasebury.

355
00:26:17.619 --> 00:26:20.330
- House Musgood.
- House Musgood.

356
00:26:20.455 --> 00:26:21.915
- And House Haigh.
- House Haigh.

357
00:26:27.796 --> 00:26:31.382
They don't have enough men between them
to raid a pantry.

358
00:26:32.258 --> 00:26:34.177
Westeros is not the world. Your Grace.

359
00:26:34.219 --> 00:26:36.012
We need to look east for ships and men.

360
00:26:36.096 --> 00:26:39.349
10.000 skilled soldiers
fight for the Golden Company.

361
00:26:39.432 --> 00:26:41.494
- The Golden Company?
- They've never broken a contract.

362
00:26:41.518 --> 00:26:42.519
They're sellswords.

363
00:26:42.602 --> 00:26:44.413
We're willing to use blood magic
to put you on the throne.

364
00:26:44.437 --> 00:26:46.439
but we're not willing to pay men to fight?

365
00:26:46.523 --> 00:26:48.858
Now the Red Woman's magic is real.

366
00:26:48.900 --> 00:26:51.027
Her visions and prophecies may be. too.

367
00:26:51.111 --> 00:26:53.947
but I've never heard of visions
and prophecies winning a war.

368
00:26:54.030 --> 00:26:56.366
Soldiers win wars. Soldiers on the ground.

369
00:26:56.407 --> 00:26:57.659
It's dirty on the ground.

370
00:26:57.700 --> 00:26:58.827
We don't have any gold.

371
00:26:59.619 --> 00:27:00.662
Not yet.

372
00:27:05.166 --> 00:27:09.129
If I do not press my claim.
my claim will be forgotten.

373
00:27:09.212 --> 00:27:12.590
I will not become a page
in someone else's history book.

374
00:27:13.716 --> 00:27:15.844
I'm running out of time. Ser Davos.

375
00:27:16.719 --> 00:27:18.888
Which means you're running out of time.

376
00:27:24.477 --> 00:27:25.562
You're late.

377
00:27:25.645 --> 00:27:27.230
I'm sorry. Princess.

378
00:27:27.272 --> 00:27:28.857
I thought you weren't coming.

379
00:27:28.898 --> 00:27:31.109
The Hand of the King
doesn't have much leisure time.

380
00:27:31.693 --> 00:27:34.863
You won't be a very good Hand if you
see the word knight and say "ka-nigit."

381
00:27:34.904 --> 00:27:36.906
That happened once. weeks ago.

382
00:27:36.948 --> 00:27:38.867
You're your father's daughter. no mistake.

383
00:27:38.908 --> 00:27:40.785
Bloody relentless. the both of you.

384
00:27:40.910 --> 00:27:43.413
It's a new one today. Lots of tricky words.

385
00:27:43.454 --> 00:27:45.582
But I think you can manage.

386
00:27:47.834 --> 00:27:49.919
You'll never read well
if you move your lips.

387
00:27:50.003 --> 00:27:52.088
That's how children do it.

388
00:27:57.260 --> 00:28:01.514
"The Life and Adventures of Elyo Grivas

389
00:28:01.598 --> 00:28:03.725
"First Sword of Braavos."

390
00:28:04.058 --> 00:28:05.852
Thank you very much.

391
00:28:06.144 --> 00:28:09.063
I like this one.
It's full of swordfights and pirates.

392
00:28:09.480 --> 00:28:12.650
- You were a pirate once.
- No. I was a smuggler.

393
00:28:12.942 --> 00:28:14.027
What's the difference?

394
00:28:14.277 --> 00:28:16.779
If you're a famous smuggler.
you're not doing it right.

395
00:28:17.447 --> 00:28:19.449
My father says a criminal is a criminal.

396
00:28:19.616 --> 00:28:23.369
Your father lacks an appreciation
of the finer points of bad behaviour.

397
00:28:24.287 --> 00:28:25.705
So do the Braavosi.

398
00:28:25.788 --> 00:28:27.348
- You've sailed to Braavos?
- Of course.

399
00:28:27.373 --> 00:28:30.293
Almost got beheaded by
a First Sword of Braavos.

400
00:28:30.752 --> 00:28:34.631
I tried to explain to him
the difference between pirates and smugglers.

401
00:28:34.714 --> 00:28:37.674
but he didn't seem any more interested
in the distinction than your father.

402
00:28:38.301 --> 00:28:40.261
I suppose if you work
for the Iron Bank of Braavos

403
00:28:40.303 --> 00:28:42.722
and each one of your gold barges
is worth half a kingdom.

404
00:28:42.931 --> 00:28:47.018
you tend not to be overly concerned
with the kind of distinction...

405
00:29:05.119 --> 00:29:07.413
- What was that for?
- I need you to write a message.

406
00:29:07.497 --> 00:29:09.499
You should write it yourself.
It's good practice.

407
00:29:09.582 --> 00:29:11.459
It's too important for me.

408
00:29:11.501 --> 00:29:14.462
I need a smart person to do it. Go on.

409
00:29:14.504 --> 00:29:18.633
To the offices of the Iron Bank of Braavos.

410
00:29:18.675 --> 00:29:22.262
from Stannis Baratheon.
the one true king of Westeros.

411
00:29:22.345 --> 00:29:23.846
But that's not you.

412
00:29:23.888 --> 00:29:25.556
I need to get their attention.

413
00:29:25.640 --> 00:29:28.184
Go. Write.

414
00:29:38.236 --> 00:29:40.488
He's seen some adventures. hasn't he?

415
00:30:00.174 --> 00:30:03.344
- Precious little thing.
- Thank you.

416
00:30:03.386 --> 00:30:06.180
- What's his name?
- Sam.

417
00:30:06.222 --> 00:30:07.890
Lovely.

418
00:30:08.725 --> 00:30:10.768
- That the daddy?
- No.

419
00:30:10.893 --> 00:30:12.228
Where's the daddy?

420
00:30:13.354 --> 00:30:14.856
He's dead.

421
00:30:16.649 --> 00:30:18.401
Where you from?

422
00:30:20.111 --> 00:30:21.571
North of here.

423
00:30:21.654 --> 00:30:23.740
North of here?

424
00:30:27.327 --> 00:30:29.954
You a fucking wildling?

425
00:30:30.413 --> 00:30:33.249
- Only room and board?
- That's right.

426
00:30:33.333 --> 00:30:36.961
She'll clean and cook
and look after the other girls' babies.

427
00:30:37.962 --> 00:30:40.423
Could find other work for her. too.

428
00:30:40.465 --> 00:30:42.467
- No other work.
- There'd be money.

429
00:30:42.550 --> 00:30:44.093
Give you a piece of it.

430
00:30:44.218 --> 00:30:46.929
No other work.

431
00:31:08.409 --> 00:31:11.079
I promise to come back and visit
whenever I can.

432
00:31:14.415 --> 00:31:16.626
You'll be safer here.

433
00:31:16.667 --> 00:31:18.503
Who's gonna protect you
at Castle Black? Me?

434
00:31:20.004 --> 00:31:21.798
You protected me north of the Wall.

435
00:31:21.881 --> 00:31:23.800
This is different.

436
00:31:23.883 --> 00:31:27.303
They're brothers of the Night's Watch.
and I can't just stab them in the back.

437
00:31:27.387 --> 00:31:30.306
And I can't run away.
which is what we did at Craster's.

438
00:31:32.517 --> 00:31:33.810
You have to trust me.

439
00:31:35.311 --> 00:31:36.687
It's for the best.

440
00:31:42.151 --> 00:31:43.403
Best for you.

441
00:31:43.945 --> 00:31:45.822
Oh. Gilly.

442
00:31:47.949 --> 00:31:49.117
Please don't...

443
00:32:22.316 --> 00:32:24.360
Greedy.

444
00:32:30.783 --> 00:32:32.577
No?

445
00:32:32.660 --> 00:32:36.372
I'm sorry. You're lovely.
I just never acquired the taste.

446
00:32:36.414 --> 00:32:38.374
You're calling my beauty an acquired taste?

447
00:32:39.292 --> 00:32:42.587
That's quite all right. lover.
There's more for you.

448
00:32:45.631 --> 00:32:47.675
Your loss.

449
00:32:53.014 --> 00:32:56.809
You like them both the same? Boys and girls?

450
00:32:56.893 --> 00:32:59.520
- Does that surprise you?
- Everyone has a preference.

451
00:32:59.604 --> 00:33:02.190
Then everyone is missing
half the world's pleasure.

452
00:33:03.733 --> 00:33:07.236
The gods made that. and it delights me.

453
00:33:07.278 --> 00:33:08.988
The gods made this.

454
00:33:09.906 --> 00:33:11.073
and it delights me.

455
00:33:11.908 --> 00:33:14.160
When it comes to war. I fight for Dorne.

456
00:33:14.243 --> 00:33:17.914
When it comes to love. I don't choose sides.

457
00:33:17.955 --> 00:33:20.166
I hope I have as much stamina
when I'm your age.

458
00:33:20.249 --> 00:33:21.959
What are you. 25?

459
00:33:22.293 --> 00:33:23.336
Children.

460
00:33:25.630 --> 00:33:29.467
Someday. if you're lucky.
you will wake up and realise you are old.

461
00:33:29.842 --> 00:33:31.719
That pretty ass of yours will sag.

462
00:33:31.761 --> 00:33:34.972
your belly will grow soft.
and your back will ache in the night.

463
00:33:35.056 --> 00:33:37.934
and grey hairs will sprout from your ears.

464
00:33:39.268 --> 00:33:41.395
No one will want you any more.

465
00:33:41.562 --> 00:33:44.565
Make sure you've fucked your fill
before that day.

466
00:33:46.067 --> 00:33:47.652
Did you?

467
00:33:48.361 --> 00:33:51.447
He is a prince of Dorne.

468
00:33:51.489 --> 00:33:56.786
Girls and boys will line up to fuck him
till the day he dies.

469
00:33:59.455 --> 00:34:02.542
They will all have to line up behind you.

470
00:34:08.089 --> 00:34:10.550
- Prince Oberyn.
- Lord Tywin.

471
00:34:10.633 --> 00:34:12.552
May we have the room?

472
00:34:16.305 --> 00:34:17.705
Call my name if you need me. lover.

473
00:34:29.652 --> 00:34:31.028
Would you like to sit?

474
00:34:31.487 --> 00:34:33.030
No. thank you.

475
00:34:33.739 --> 00:34:36.826
- Some wine?
- No. thank you.

476
00:34:38.661 --> 00:34:40.705
I'm sorry about your grandson.

477
00:34:40.788 --> 00:34:41.831
Are you?

478
00:34:41.872 --> 00:34:45.501
I don't believe that a child is responsible
for the sins of his father.

479
00:34:46.586 --> 00:34:49.005
Or his grandfather.

480
00:34:49.046 --> 00:34:50.590
An awful way to die.

481
00:34:51.632 --> 00:34:52.842
Which way is that?

482
00:34:53.509 --> 00:34:56.137
Are you interrogating me. Lord Tywin?

483
00:34:56.178 --> 00:34:57.638
Some believe the King choked.

484
00:34:58.097 --> 00:35:02.643
Some believe the sky is blue because
we live inside the eye of a blue-eyed giant.

485
00:35:04.812 --> 00:35:06.856
The King was poisoned.

486
00:35:07.440 --> 00:35:09.984
I hear you studied poisons at the Citadel.

487
00:35:10.067 --> 00:35:12.403
I did. This is why I know.

488
00:35:12.486 --> 00:35:15.364
Your hatred for my family
is rather well-known.

489
00:35:16.198 --> 00:35:18.868
You arrive at the capital.
an expert in poisoning.

490
00:35:18.909 --> 00:35:22.705
some days later
my grandson dies of poisoning.

491
00:35:22.830 --> 00:35:24.206
Rather suspicious.

492
00:35:24.373 --> 00:35:26.042
Why haven't you thrown me in a dungeon?

493
00:35:26.125 --> 00:35:29.795
You spoke with Tyrion in this very brothel
on the day that you arrived.

494
00:35:30.921 --> 00:35:34.216
- What did you discuss?
- You think we conspired together?

495
00:35:34.258 --> 00:35:35.593
What did you discuss?

496
00:35:35.718 --> 00:35:38.596
The death of my sister.

497
00:35:39.096 --> 00:35:40.723
For which you blame me.

498
00:35:40.806 --> 00:35:43.225
She was raped and murdered
by the Mountain.

499
00:35:43.267 --> 00:35:45.728
The Mountain follows your orders.

500
00:35:45.811 --> 00:35:47.271
Of course I blame you.

501
00:35:47.396 --> 00:35:50.358
Here I stand unarmed. unguarded.

502
00:35:50.399 --> 00:35:51.567
Should I be concerned?

503
00:35:51.651 --> 00:35:55.071
You are unarmed and unguarded
because you know me better than that.

504
00:35:56.322 --> 00:35:57.698
I am a man of reason.

505
00:35:58.032 --> 00:36:01.410
If I cut your throat today.
I will be drawn and quartered tomorrow.

506
00:36:01.494 --> 00:36:05.247
Men at war commit all kinds of crimes
without their superiors' knowledge.

507
00:36:05.331 --> 00:36:07.792
So you deny involvement in Elia's murder?

508
00:36:08.918 --> 00:36:10.586
Categorically.

509
00:36:19.804 --> 00:36:22.056
I would like to speak with the Mountain.

510
00:36:22.348 --> 00:36:24.600
I'm sure he would enjoy speaking with you.

511
00:36:24.684 --> 00:36:27.603
He might not enjoy it
as much as he thinks he would.

512
00:36:29.647 --> 00:36:32.525
I could arrange for this meeting.

513
00:36:33.067 --> 00:36:36.404
But you want something in return.

514
00:36:36.946 --> 00:36:41.117
There will be a trial for my son
and. as custom dictates.

515
00:36:41.158 --> 00:36:43.953
three judges will render a verdict.

516
00:36:44.036 --> 00:36:45.454
I will preside.

517
00:36:45.538 --> 00:36:48.624
Mace Tyrell will serve as the second judge.

518
00:36:49.125 --> 00:36:50.835
I would like you to be the third.

519
00:36:51.419 --> 00:36:52.795
Why?

520
00:36:52.837 --> 00:36:56.632
Not long ago.
the Tyrells sided with Renly Baratheon.

521
00:36:56.716 --> 00:36:59.385
Declared themselves enemies of the throne.

522
00:36:59.468 --> 00:37:01.554
Now they are our strongest allies.

523
00:37:01.637 --> 00:37:04.140
Well. you made the Tyrell girl a queen.

524
00:37:04.223 --> 00:37:07.435
Asking me to judge at your son's trial
isn't quite as tempting.

525
00:37:07.893 --> 00:37:11.355
I would also invite you
to sit on the Small Council

526
00:37:11.439 --> 00:37:14.942
to serve as one of
the new king's principal advisors.

527
00:37:20.906 --> 00:37:25.494
I never realised
you had such respect for Dorne. Lord Tywin.

528
00:37:25.536 --> 00:37:29.206
We are not the Seven Kingdoms
until Dorne returns to the fold.

529
00:37:29.540 --> 00:37:32.918
The King is dead.
The Greyjoys are in open rebellion.

530
00:37:33.294 --> 00:37:36.046
A wildling army marches on the Wall.

531
00:37:36.130 --> 00:37:40.384
And in the east.
a Targaryen girl has three dragons.

532
00:37:42.845 --> 00:37:45.765
Before long.
she will turn her eyes to Westeros.

533
00:37:46.182 --> 00:37:51.479
Only the Dornish managed to resist
Aegon Targaryen and his dragons.

534
00:37:52.271 --> 00:37:54.190
You're saying you need us?

535
00:37:56.025 --> 00:37:58.444
That must be hard for you to admit.

536
00:37:59.528 --> 00:38:01.572
We need each other.

537
00:38:02.364 --> 00:38:05.201
You help me serve justice to
the King's assassins.

538
00:38:05.284 --> 00:38:08.037
and I will help you serve justice to Elia's.

539
00:38:27.723 --> 00:38:28.724
Podrick.

540
00:38:30.601 --> 00:38:31.936
Apologies for the stench.

541
00:38:32.019 --> 00:38:34.339
I brought you some wine. my lord.
but they took it from me.

542
00:38:34.396 --> 00:38:35.898
A noble effort.

543
00:38:35.981 --> 00:38:38.234
They didn't find the candles. though.

544
00:38:38.984 --> 00:38:40.778
A quill. some parchment.

545
00:38:40.861 --> 00:38:43.531
duck sausage. almonds.

546
00:38:44.490 --> 00:38:46.659
and some hard cheese.

547
00:38:46.742 --> 00:38:48.285
You're a good lad.

548
00:38:49.036 --> 00:38:50.579
Any word of Shae?

549
00:38:50.913 --> 00:38:52.248
I've heard nothing. my lord.

550
00:38:52.873 --> 00:38:54.750
I suppose that's a good thing.

551
00:38:56.418 --> 00:38:59.630
What are they saying about me out there?

552
00:38:59.713 --> 00:39:03.759
You're to stand trial in a fortnight
for murdering the King.

553
00:39:04.885 --> 00:39:07.763
- Do you believe I murdered Joffrey?
- No. my lord.

554
00:39:08.681 --> 00:39:09.723
You didn't?

555
00:39:10.140 --> 00:39:12.434
Gods. no.

556
00:39:12.768 --> 00:39:16.772
The world is a better place without him.
but I had nothing to do with it.

557
00:39:17.898 --> 00:39:21.610
I would like to think
if I were arranging a royal assassination.

558
00:39:21.652 --> 00:39:23.755
I'd plan it in such a way that
I wouldn't be standing there.

559
00:39:23.779 --> 00:39:25.573
gawking like a fool when the King died.

560
00:39:28.492 --> 00:39:30.286
Trial in a fortnight.

561
00:39:31.078 --> 00:39:33.289
Have they announced the judges yet?

562
00:39:36.000 --> 00:39:38.669
- Your father.
- Of course.

563
00:39:39.670 --> 00:39:41.839
Mace Tyrell.

564
00:39:41.922 --> 00:39:44.717
Who will vote exactly
as my father tells him to vote.

565
00:39:44.842 --> 00:39:47.887
- And Prince Oberyn of Dorne.
- Oberyn?

566
00:39:50.097 --> 00:39:51.891
Give it to my father.

567
00:39:51.974 --> 00:39:54.184
He never fails to take advantage
of a family tragedy.

568
00:39:54.268 --> 00:39:57.980
I'm supposed to get a list of names
from you. my lord.

569
00:39:58.022 --> 00:40:00.524
Anyone who might testify on your behalf.

570
00:40:00.608 --> 00:40:02.234
Oh. I can call my own witnesses?

571
00:40:03.152 --> 00:40:04.653
How generous of them.

572
00:40:04.737 --> 00:40:06.530
Very well. my wife. Sansa.

573
00:40:06.614 --> 00:40:08.490
My lord. she's gone.

574
00:40:08.741 --> 00:40:11.702
- Gone?
- No one's seen her since the wedding.

575
00:40:14.830 --> 00:40:17.416
You don't think she...

576
00:40:20.794 --> 00:40:24.173
No one had more cause to kill Joffrey
than Sansa.

577
00:40:24.256 --> 00:40:26.258
but the girl is no assassin.

578
00:40:26.342 --> 00:40:29.470
Whoever killed the King
wanted me to lose my head for it.

579
00:40:29.511 --> 00:40:33.015
And with my wife's disappearance.
it makes me seem that much more guilty.

580
00:40:33.891 --> 00:40:35.935
- Podrick.
- Yes. my lord?

581
00:40:36.018 --> 00:40:37.537
- They'll be following you now.
- Who will?

582
00:40:37.561 --> 00:40:40.272
I don't know. They. The ominous they.

583
00:40:40.356 --> 00:40:43.359
The man pulling the strings.
Or woman. My father.

584
00:40:44.193 --> 00:40:46.904
Maybe Joffrey was too much work for him.

585
00:40:46.987 --> 00:40:49.740
Sweet Tommen will be
so much easier to handle.

586
00:40:50.491 --> 00:40:55.037
Whenever something bad happens to me.
I assume it's my sister that had a hand in it.

587
00:40:55.412 --> 00:40:57.539
But say what you will of Cersei.

588
00:40:57.581 --> 00:40:59.208
she loves her children.

589
00:40:59.333 --> 00:41:03.212
She is the only one I'm certain
had nothing to do with this murder.

590
00:41:03.671 --> 00:41:07.967
Which makes it unique
as King's Landing murders go.

591
00:41:08.050 --> 00:41:10.094
Any other witnesses. my lord?

592
00:41:10.886 --> 00:41:12.846
Varys could vouch for me. if he dared.

593
00:41:12.888 --> 00:41:14.928
He's already been called
as a witness for the Queen.

594
00:41:14.974 --> 00:41:17.893
Of course. Fetch Bronn.
I have a job for him.

595
00:41:17.977 --> 00:41:19.704
I've already asked. my lord.
They won't let him see you.

596
00:41:19.728 --> 00:41:20.771
Why not?

597
00:41:20.854 --> 00:41:23.399
They say he's a known cutthroat
and your close associate.

598
00:41:23.482 --> 00:41:24.984
He's under investigation himself.

599
00:41:25.067 --> 00:41:28.362
And my brother?
Will they at least allow me to see Jaime?

600
00:41:28.404 --> 00:41:29.488
I'll ask. my lord.

601
00:41:44.878 --> 00:41:47.381
There's something else. my lord.

602
00:41:47.423 --> 00:41:50.676
A man. I didn't know his face.

603
00:41:50.759 --> 00:41:52.594
he came to ask if I'd testify against you.

604
00:41:53.512 --> 00:41:56.223
Said I'd be named Ser Podrick Payne

605
00:41:56.265 --> 00:41:59.601
if I told the judges
you'd bought a poison called the strangler.

606
00:41:59.935 --> 00:42:01.979
Ser Podrick Payne?

607
00:42:02.062 --> 00:42:06.108
- Has a nice ring to it. What did you tell him?
- I didn't tell them anything. my lord.

608
00:42:07.776 --> 00:42:09.528
Are you going to accept their offer?

609
00:42:10.738 --> 00:42:13.532
- My lord.
- Testifying against me wasn't a suggestion.

610
00:42:13.615 --> 00:42:16.910
If they can't tempt you with honey.
they'll choose something less sweet.

611
00:42:16.952 --> 00:42:20.789
- You've been good to me. my lord.
- Pod. the trial's in a fortnight.

612
00:42:20.831 --> 00:42:22.458
They'll want an answer before that.

613
00:42:22.583 --> 00:42:24.143
I already gave them an answer. my lord.

614
00:42:26.086 --> 00:42:28.922
I will not have you dying on my behalf.

615
00:42:28.964 --> 00:42:30.215
Do you hear me?

616
00:42:30.299 --> 00:42:32.968
If I have to take that long walk to
the executioner's block.

617
00:42:33.052 --> 00:42:35.471
I don't want to see
your head already mounted.

618
00:42:35.554 --> 00:42:38.223
- My lord.
- Pod. I am giving you an order.

619
00:42:39.308 --> 00:42:42.770
Go and find my brother. Tell him I need him.

620
00:42:43.312 --> 00:42:46.065
And get yourself out of King's Landing
before it's too late.

621
00:42:47.399 --> 00:42:48.984
Pod!

622
00:42:49.276 --> 00:42:50.736
This is farewell.

623
00:42:53.614 --> 00:42:55.783
Farewell. my lord.

624
00:43:00.579 --> 00:43:01.830
Pod.

625
00:43:06.001 --> 00:43:09.171
There has never lived a more loyal squire.

626
00:43:33.112 --> 00:43:34.530
Mother says it's time to eat.

627
00:43:34.571 --> 00:43:38.200
What's she got boiling? Wait. Let me guess.

628
00:43:38.283 --> 00:43:39.493
Potatoes.

629
00:43:39.535 --> 00:43:42.830
No one boils a potato better than your mom.

630
00:43:42.871 --> 00:43:44.331
She got...

631
00:43:45.624 --> 00:43:46.667
The wildlings!

632
00:43:47.167 --> 00:43:48.544
Guymon!

633
00:43:50.379 --> 00:43:51.839
Hide.

634
00:43:51.880 --> 00:43:53.841
- Hide!
- Run!

635
00:44:45.100 --> 00:44:48.687
- You know how to get to Castle Black?
- Yes.

636
00:44:56.445 --> 00:44:58.697
Those your parents?

637
00:44:59.948 --> 00:45:01.742
Open your eyes.

638
00:45:02.910 --> 00:45:04.620
I'm going to eat them.

639
00:45:05.329 --> 00:45:06.663
Do you hear me?

640
00:45:06.830 --> 00:45:09.374
I'm going to eat your dead mama

641
00:45:09.458 --> 00:45:12.211
and your dead papa.

642
00:45:13.337 --> 00:45:16.131
Go tell the crows at Castle Black.

643
00:45:25.182 --> 00:45:28.036
We need to teach them a lesson
about the way we deal with their kind.

644
00:45:28.060 --> 00:45:29.102
Aye! Aye!

645
00:45:29.186 --> 00:45:33.190
Three dozen bodies with
slit throats tossed off the top of the Wall.

646
00:45:33.273 --> 00:45:35.359
- Seems like that would be a good lesson.
- Aye!

647
00:45:35.442 --> 00:45:37.986
If we go after them.
we'll be giving them what they want.

648
00:45:38.570 --> 00:45:42.449
They want to draw us out.
pick us off a few at a time.

649
00:45:42.491 --> 00:45:45.244
We have just over 100 men.

650
00:45:45.410 --> 00:45:48.580
And that's including stewards and builders.

651
00:45:49.331 --> 00:45:52.584
And me. We can't afford
to lose a single man.

652
00:45:53.252 --> 00:45:56.964
We must remember our first responsibility.

653
00:45:57.464 --> 00:46:00.133
We are the watchers on the Wall.

654
00:46:01.593 --> 00:46:03.193
There's got to be a way to protect them.

655
00:46:04.596 --> 00:46:07.307
You're a champion of the common people.
Lord Snow.

656
00:46:07.349 --> 00:46:10.143
What do you say
to Brother Pyp's proposition?

657
00:46:14.481 --> 00:46:16.858
Mance Rayder is coming.

658
00:46:18.527 --> 00:46:20.779
If the wildlings breach the Wall.

659
00:46:20.862 --> 00:46:23.657
they'll roll over everything
and everyone for 1.000 miles

660
00:46:23.699 --> 00:46:25.499
before they reach
an army that can stop them.

661
00:46:29.162 --> 00:46:31.164
We need to shore up Castle Black

662
00:46:32.207 --> 00:46:34.584
and defend the Wall.

663
00:46:35.711 --> 00:46:37.879
That is our job.

664
00:46:44.386 --> 00:46:45.846
Rangers returning.

665
00:46:52.769 --> 00:46:54.479
Help him.

666
00:46:56.106 --> 00:46:58.984
Thought you'd have blue eyes by now.

667
00:47:02.654 --> 00:47:04.031
What took you so long?

668
00:47:04.406 --> 00:47:06.616
- We were held up.
- By what?

669
00:47:07.117 --> 00:47:08.118
Chains.

670
00:47:08.201 --> 00:47:11.788
We were guests of the mutineers
at Craster's Keep.

671
00:47:11.872 --> 00:47:14.583
- And the mutineers stayed?
- They're not going anywhere.

672
00:47:14.624 --> 00:47:17.753
They've got Craster's food and his wives.

673
00:47:17.794 --> 00:47:21.423
Poor girls.
Never thought they'd miss their daddy.

674
00:47:21.465 --> 00:47:23.091
Karl's running things now.

675
00:47:23.175 --> 00:47:25.635
He's the one who put a knife
through Craster's mouth.

676
00:47:25.719 --> 00:47:27.319
We need to ride north and kill them all.

677
00:47:27.387 --> 00:47:28.972
We just went over this. boy.

678
00:47:29.056 --> 00:47:31.516
- Justice can wait.
- It's not about justice.

679
00:47:33.602 --> 00:47:38.106
I told the wildlings
we had over 1.000 men at Castle Black alone.

680
00:47:39.149 --> 00:47:41.526
Karl and the others know the truth
as well as we do.

681
00:47:43.111 --> 00:47:45.548
How long do you think they'll keep
that information to themselves

682
00:47:45.572 --> 00:47:48.575
when the wildlings are
peeling their fingernails off?

683
00:47:49.451 --> 00:47:52.662
Mance has all he needs to crush us.
he just doesn't know it yet.

684
00:47:52.788 --> 00:47:55.332
As soon as he gets his hands on them.
he will.

685
00:47:56.875 --> 00:47:58.752
Then he'll throw his full strength at us.

686
00:47:59.419 --> 00:48:02.214
And even if every one of us
kills 100 wildlings.

687
00:48:02.297 --> 00:48:04.883
there's still not a thing
we can do to stop them.

688
00:48:07.260 --> 00:48:09.471
I don't think I can kill 100 wildlings.

689
00:49:12.492 --> 00:49:14.619
Are they attacking?

690
00:49:15.078 --> 00:49:17.205
A single rider.

691
00:49:17.914 --> 00:49:20.667
A champion of Meereen.

692
00:49:20.709 --> 00:49:23.712
They want you to send your own champion
against him.

693
00:49:49.696 --> 00:49:51.531
What is he doing?

694
00:49:51.573 --> 00:49:54.284
I believe he means to...

695
00:50:01.416 --> 00:50:04.878
He says that
we're an army of men without man parts.

696
00:50:05.212 --> 00:50:07.589
He claims you are no woman at all.
but a man who

697
00:50:08.924 --> 00:50:11.051
hides his cock in his own arsehole.

698
00:50:11.551 --> 00:50:14.095
Ignore him. Your Grace.
These are meaningless words.

699
00:50:14.179 --> 00:50:18.433
They're not meaningless if half the city
you intend to take is listening to them.

700
00:50:21.770 --> 00:50:24.648
I have something to say
to the people of Meereen.

701
00:50:25.941 --> 00:50:27.692
First. I will need this one to be quiet.

702
00:50:29.861 --> 00:50:30.862
Do I have a champion?

703
00:50:31.363 --> 00:50:34.366
Allow me this honour. Mother of Dragons.

704
00:50:34.783 --> 00:50:36.785
I will not disappoint you.

705
00:50:37.244 --> 00:50:38.804
You are the commander of the Unsullied.

706
00:50:39.287 --> 00:50:40.789
I cannot risk you.

707
00:50:41.289 --> 00:50:44.626
Your Grace. I've won more single combats
than any man alive.

708
00:50:44.709 --> 00:50:46.920
Which is why you must remain by my side.

709
00:50:47.629 --> 00:50:50.966
I've been by your side
longer than any of them. Khaleesi.

710
00:50:51.007 --> 00:50:52.592
Let me stand for you today as well.

711
00:50:52.842 --> 00:50:54.553
You are my most trusted advisor.

712
00:50:54.636 --> 00:50:57.514
my most valued general.
and my dearest friend.

713
00:50:57.597 --> 00:50:59.307
I will not gamble with your life.

714
00:50:59.516 --> 00:51:01.977
I was the last to join your army.

715
00:51:02.018 --> 00:51:04.187
I'm not your general
or a member of your Queensguard

716
00:51:04.271 --> 00:51:05.671
or the commander of your Unsullied.

717
00:51:05.814 --> 00:51:08.984
My mother was a whore. I come from nothing.

718
00:51:09.067 --> 00:51:10.986
I will return to nothing.

719
00:51:12.654 --> 00:51:14.823
Let me kill this man for you.

720
00:51:15.991 --> 00:51:17.367
Very well.

721
00:51:17.450 --> 00:51:18.827
You have quite an audience.

722
00:51:19.828 --> 00:51:22.330
Make it worth their while.

723
00:51:23.415 --> 00:51:25.041
He is very brave. Your Grace.

724
00:51:25.125 --> 00:51:26.459
Yes. win or lose.

725
00:51:26.793 --> 00:51:28.587
as long as the whole city is watching.

726
00:51:40.849 --> 00:51:42.309
You sure you don't want a horse?

727
00:51:42.726 --> 00:51:44.060
Why would I want a horse?

728
00:51:44.519 --> 00:51:46.646
Horses are faster than men.

729
00:51:47.439 --> 00:51:49.441
Horses are dumber than men.

730
00:53:08.770 --> 00:53:11.272
I am Daenerys Stormborn.

731
00:53:15.568 --> 00:53:19.280
Your Masters may have
told you lies about me.

732
00:53:19.322 --> 00:53:21.366
or they may have told you nothing.

733
00:53:21.616 --> 00:53:22.951
It does not matter.

734
00:53:23.993 --> 00:53:25.954
I have nothing to say to them.

735
00:53:26.663 --> 00:53:28.540
I speak only to you.

736
00:53:30.959 --> 00:53:32.711
First. I went to Astapor.

737
00:53:32.836 --> 00:53:34.963
Those who were slaves in Astapor.

738
00:53:35.422 --> 00:53:37.590
now stand behind me.

739
00:53:38.717 --> 00:53:39.968
free.

740
00:53:41.469 --> 00:53:43.638
Next I went to Yunkai.

741
00:53:43.680 --> 00:53:45.724
Those who were slaves in Yunkai.

742
00:53:46.599 --> 00:53:48.810
now stand behind me.

743
00:53:49.686 --> 00:53:50.854
free.

744
00:53:53.314 --> 00:53:55.483
Now I have come to Meereen.

745
00:53:56.985 --> 00:54:00.321
I am not your enemy.

746
00:54:00.363 --> 00:54:03.867
Your enemy is beside you.

747
00:54:04.617 --> 00:54:09.330
Your enemy steals and murders your children.

748
00:54:10.498 --> 00:54:14.627
Your enemy has nothing for you
but chains and suffering

749
00:54:15.003 --> 00:54:16.880
and commands.

750
00:54:19.007 --> 00:54:20.842
I did not bring you commands.

751
00:54:21.926 --> 00:54:23.636
I bring you a choice.

752
00:54:24.846 --> 00:54:28.016
And I bring your enemies what they deserve.

753
00:54:31.019 --> 00:54:32.645
Forward!

754
00:54:44.282 --> 00:54:45.366
Fire!

755
00:54:46.305 --> 00:55:46.593
